## §4 Where I think the reviewer is wrong (NOT applied)

1. b17 / a17 (U+200B). Part b asks to delete every U+200B and the blank lines they hold. That is not a Greek-quality defect
   and the checker forbids it (§2). Part a's reviewer is right that it is a pipeline artefact.
2. b33 (018 §4 "contract-design advice"). The reviewer already says not to change the Greek; recorded here so the English
   lane picks it up.
3. a18 says the German double form is in "5 places in the pack (contact §1, §3, §4 and privacy §3)". Only 3 exist on disk
   (about "Τρία πράγματα", contact "Η γλώσσα της σελίδας …", contact "Τι δεν υπόσχεται η σελίδα αυτή"); the other pack
   sentences already read «συμβουλευτική με δικηγόρο». All 3 real ones are fixed.
4. a8 says "≈40 places in part a, ≈19 more in 010–018" (≈59). The real figure over the columns *and* the guidance pack is
   150. The higher number is the sweep, not a disagreement — recorded so the count is not mistaken for over-editing.
5. b36 suggests «η βολή του διαχειριστή». «Βολή» is colloquial and clashes with the register of 016; the point (convenience,
   not discretion) is carried by «η ευκολία», which is what was written.
6. a1's suggested «διακρίνει την προγαμιαία περιουσία … από την περιουσία που αποκτήθηκε …» was adopted, but the reviewer's
   §6 heading fix needed «προγαμιαία περιουσία» (not «περιουσιακά στοιχεία») to stay inside one heading line — noted so the
   next round does not read it as an inconsistency.


